Overview
This lab introduced the role of a Security Operations Center (SOC) and how cybersecurity teams work together to protect organizational assets.

The exercise focused on SOC responsibilities, analyst roles, incident escalation, team collaboration, and enterprise security operations.

Learning Objectives
Understand the purpose and responsibilities of the Blue Team.
Explore the structure of a cybersecurity department.
Identify the responsibilities of SOC Level 1, Level 2, and Level 3 analysts.
Understand the roles of Red Team, Blue Team, and GRC teams.
Differentiate between internal SOC operations and MSSPs.
Understand incident management and escalation procedures.
