SOC Roles and Responsibilities
Role	Responsibility
SOC Level 1 Analyst	Monitor alerts, perform initial investigations, and escalate suspicious activity.
SOC Level 2 Analyst	Conduct deeper investigations and analyze security events.
SOC Level 3 Analyst	Handle advanced threats and complex incidents.
SOC Manager	Manage SOC operations and analyst activities.
CISO	Define cybersecurity strategy and security policies.
Red Team	Simulate attacks to identify weaknesses.
Blue Team	Monitor, detect, and respond to threats.
GRC Team	Manage governance, risk, and compliance activities.
Incident Response Team	Coordinate containment, eradication, and recovery efforts.
Practical Exercises
Cybersecurity Department Structure
Examined the organizational hierarchy of a security department.
Identified responsibilities across SOC analyst levels.
Compared internal SOC teams with MSSPs.
Reviewed incident assignment procedures.
Evaluated multiple simultaneous security incidents.
Enterprise Incident Management Scenario
A simulated multinational organization experienced multiple security incidents at the same time.

Acting as a CISO, the objective was to assign incidents to the appropriate security teams and specialists.

Key concepts demonstrated:

Incident classification
Incident prioritization
Escalation procedures
Team coordination
Enterprise security operations
